    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d485">

                <pb facs="0543" n="439" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg439"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.516/131: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Culbertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-06-10T00:00:00-05:00">June 10,
                            1932—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received June 11—4:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>75. Referring to my telegram No. 68 [<hi rendition="#italic">74</hi>],<anchor
                        n="10" xml:id="d485-f1"/> transmitting message of [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to</hi>] National City Bank, I suggest that this message be delivered as
                    soon as possible. Two features of the situation should be noted, first, the
                    importance of a common policy among British and American banks; second, that one
                    of the facts which must be considered in making the decision not to pay drawings
                    by the Central Bank now under the control of the revolutionary government is
                    that it may be followed by retaliation against American interests. Perhaps it
                    will be felt that this is a chance which should be taken.</p>
                <p>Minister of Finance declared tonight that the decree against foreign currency
                    deposits will be enforced and if resisted measures will be taken similar to
                    those taken against Central Bank, but we will have to await further developments
                    before we can say how seriously this declaration is to be considered. We know at
                    least that the Minister of Finance and others in the Government are
                    irresponsible and capable of measures of violence.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
